  "notes": "CONJUGATION (godan-u):\n- Negative: {付|つ}き{添|そ}わない\n- Te-form: {付|つ}き{添|そ}って\n- Past: {付|つ}き{添|そ}った\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive. Takes the particle に to mark the person being accompanied: Xに{付|つ}き{添|そ}う.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {患者|かんじゃ}に{付|つ}き{添|そ}う: to attend to a patient\n- {子供|こども}に{付|つ}き{添|そ}う: to accompany a child\n- {付|つ}き{添|そ}い: attendant, escort (noun form)\n- {付|つ}き{添|そ}い{人|にん}: caregiver, chaperone\n\nUSAGE:\nStronger than simply {一緒|いっしょ}に{行|い}く (going together). Implies a duty of care or protective role, commonly used in medical and childcare contexts.",
